{"id": "wwdc2019-515", "language": "eng", "source": "https://developer.apple.com/videos/play/wwdc2019/515", "wordCount": 1230, "segments": [{"start": 13.0, "text": "Hello. My name is Jessie"}, {"start": 15.0, "text": "Berlin, and I'm here to talk"}, {"start": 17.0, "text": "about what's new in Safari."}, {"start": 20.0, "text": "We have three topics to cover"}, {"start": 21.0, "text": "today, and the most exciting one"}, {"start": 24.0, "text": "is desktop-class browsing on"}, {"start": 27.0, "text": "iPad."}, {"start": 28.0, "text": "In iOS 13, we've made a set of"}, {"start": 31.0, "text": "fundamental changes to allow"}, {"start": 33.0, "text": "iPad to browse desktop websites,"}, {"start": 35.0, "text": "and you'll notice here that I'm"}, {"start": 38.0, "text": "showing Safari View Controller."}, {"start": 40.0, "text": "It also gets these desktop"}, {"start": 41.0, "text": "websites right out of the box."}, {"start": 43.0, "text": "If you have a custom in-app web"}, {"start": 46.0, "text": "browser, or even just an app"}, {"start": 48.0, "text": "that uses WKWebView, you're"}, {"start": 50.0, "text": "going to want to check out the"}, {"start": 51.0, "text": "talk from earlier this week for"}, {"start": 53.0, "text": "detailed guidance and best"}, {"start": 54.0, "text": "practices."}, {"start": 55.0, "text": "So if you haven't already, go"}, {"start": 57.0, "text": "check it out."}, {"start": 60.0, "text": "Next up, improvements to Safari"}, {"start": 62.0, "text": "extensions."}, {"start": 64.0, "text": "We'll start with a refresher on"}, {"start": 65.0, "text": "the four different types of"}, {"start": 66.0, "text": "Safari extensions."}, {"start": 68.0, "text": "First, there are Legacy Safari"}, {"start": 72.0, "text": "extensions from macOS."}, {"start": 75.0, "text": "They were introduced in 2010"}, {"start": 77.0, "text": "with Mac OS X Snow Leopard, and"}, {"start": 79.0, "text": "deprecated last year."}, {"start": 82.0, "text": "Next, content blockers."}, {"start": 84.0, "text": "These are available for both iOS"}, {"start": 85.0, "text": "and macOS, and they're designed"}, {"start": 87.0, "text": "for speed and user privacy."}, {"start": 90.0, "text": "Third, share extensions."}, {"start": 92.0, "text": "These are also available on both"}, {"start": 94.0, "text": "iOS and macOS."}, {"start": 96.0, "text": "Once invoked by the user,"}, {"start": 97.0, "text": "they're able to run JavaScript"}, {"start": 98.0, "text": "on the webpage, and return data"}, {"start": 100.0, "text": "to your app extension."}, {"start": 102.0, "text": "And finally, Safari app"}, {"start": 105.0, "text": "extensions, available on macOS."}, {"start": 108.0, "text": "These run on web pages without"}, {"start": 109.0, "text": "user action and can be"}, {"start": 111.0, "text": "restricted to run on a single"}, {"start": 112.0, "text": "website or run everywhere."}, {"start": 114.0, "text": "Now that content blockers, share"}, {"start": 118.0, "text": "extensions, and Safari app"}, {"start": 119.0, "text": "extensions provide great"}, {"start": 121.0, "text": "extensibility options without"}, {"start": 122.0, "text": "the performance and privacy"}, {"start": 125.0, "text": "problems of Legacy Safari"}, {"start": 126.0, "text": "extensions, we are dropping"}, {"start": 129.0, "text": "support for Legacy Safari"}, {"start": 130.0, "text": "extensions in Safari 13."}, {"start": 132.0, "text": "Safari will no longer load them."}, {"start": 136.0, "text": "Today, we're going to be"}, {"start": 137.0, "text": "primarily focusing on"}, {"start": 139.0, "text": "improvements to content blockers"}, {"start": 140.0, "text": "and Safari app extensions on"}, {"start": 141.0, "text": "macOS."}, {"start": 144.0, "text": "These Safari extensions come"}, {"start": 146.0, "text": "bundled with Mac apps built in"}, {"start": 147.0, "text": "Xcode, which gives you the"}, {"start": 149.0, "text": "ability to take advantage of"}, {"start": 150.0, "text": "powerful native APIs and"}, {"start": 152.0, "text": "frameworks, as well as HTML,"}, {"start": 154.0, "text": "JavaScript, and CSS."}, {"start": 158.0, "text": "And when you install an app with"}, {"start": 159.0, "text": "a Safari app extension from the"}, {"start": 161.0, "text": "Mac App Store, your extensions"}, {"start": 163.0, "text": "show up immediately in Safari's"}, {"start": 164.0, "text": "preferences, ready for your"}, {"start": 166.0, "text": "users to turn on."}, {"start": 168.0, "text": "However, you can also distribute"}, {"start": 170.0, "text": "your app directly from your"}, {"start": 172.0, "text": "website after running it through"}, {"start": 173.0, "text": "the notarization service."}, {"start": 175.0, "text": "Notarized apps need to be"}, {"start": 176.0, "text": "launched at least once for their"}, {"start": 178.0, "text": "extension to show up in Safari."}, {"start": 180.0, "text": "We love the content blockers and"}, {"start": 184.0, "text": "Safari app extensions you have"}, {"start": 185.0, "text": "created, and we also really"}, {"start": 187.0, "text": "appreciate those of you who have"}, {"start": 189.0, "text": "filed bug reports, suggested"}, {"start": 190.0, "text": "improvements, and commented on"}, {"start": 192.0, "text": "the Safari developer forums."}, {"start": 196.0, "text": "And in response to that"}, {"start": 197.0, "text": "feedback, we've added new APIs"}, {"start": 200.0, "text": "for Safari app extensions to"}, {"start": 201.0, "text": "use."}, {"start": 204.0, "text": "Earlier this year, we built out"}, {"start": 205.0, "text": "our windows and tabs APIs."}, {"start": 207.0, "text": "Now you can navigate a tab"}, {"start": 209.0, "text": "directly from your app extension"}, {"start": 210.0, "text": "process to your full-page"}, {"start": 212.0, "text": "content, to provide extra"}, {"start": 213.0, "text": "functionality, like a dashboard."}, {"start": 215.0, "text": "You can get all the open windows"}, {"start": 218.0, "text": "and tabs to provide things like"}, {"start": 219.0, "text": "bookmarking services, and get a"}, {"start": 223.0, "text": "reference to the containing tab"}, {"start": 224.0, "text": "and window when handling a"}, {"start": 226.0, "text": "message from your injected"}, {"start": 227.0, "text": "script to do things like"}, {"start": 228.0, "text": "updating your toolbar items."}, {"start": 232.0, "text": "We've added a way for you to get"}, {"start": 233.0, "text": "the visible contents of a page."}, {"start": 235.0, "text": "You could use this, for example,"}, {"start": 237.0, "text": "to show a custom visual"}, {"start": 238.0, "text": "representation of your user's"}, {"start": 240.0, "text": "tabs."}, {"start": 241.0, "text": "And you now have more control"}, {"start": 244.0, "text": "over your UI in Safari, with the"}, {"start": 246.0, "text": "ability to programmatically show"}, {"start": 248.0, "text": "and dismiss your pop-overs when"}, {"start": 249.0, "text": "it makes the most sense for your"}, {"start": 251.0, "text": "use cases."}, {"start": 254.0, "text": "You gave us feedback about"}, {"start": 255.0, "text": "wanting to know when a page will"}, {"start": 256.0, "text": "navigate, in order to redirect"}, {"start": 258.0, "text": "for a different version of the"}, {"start": 259.0, "text": "website."}, {"start": 261.0, "text": "New in Safari 13, there's a"}, {"start": 263.0, "text": "callback that your app extension"}, {"start": 264.0, "text": "can handle to get notified of"}, {"start": 266.0, "text": "the full redirect chain."}, {"start": 267.0, "text": "For those of you who developed"}, {"start": 270.0, "text": "content blockers, we heard that"}, {"start": 272.0, "text": "you really want a way to show"}, {"start": 273.0, "text": "off to your users just how much"}, {"start": 275.0, "text": "you're helping protect them"}, {"start": 276.0, "text": "against tracking, crypto"}, {"start": 278.0, "text": "currency mining, or other"}, {"start": 280.0, "text": "unnecessary scripts."}, {"start": 281.0, "text": "So we're excited to announce, in"}, {"start": 284.0, "text": "Safari 13, that you can now"}, {"start": 286.0, "text": "associate your content blocker"}, {"start": 287.0, "text": "with your Safari app extension,"}, {"start": 289.0, "text": "so that it can get notified when"}, {"start": 291.0, "text": "content is blocked."}, {"start": 294.0, "text": "Users will be able to just turn"}, {"start": 295.0, "text": "on the Safari app extension if"}, {"start": 297.0, "text": "they want to get statistics from"}, {"start": 298.0, "text": "you on what you've blocked or"}, {"start": 300.0, "text": "keep it off if they want the"}, {"start": 301.0, "text": "most private experience."}, {"start": 303.0, "text": "I've gone through these APIs"}, {"start": 307.0, "text": "pretty quickly here, but we've"}, {"start": 308.0, "text": "created a video that you can"}, {"start": 310.0, "text": "watch to learn more in-depth how"}, {"start": 311.0, "text": "to adopt them."}, {"start": 313.0, "text": "Check it out in the WWDC app."}, {"start": 317.0, "text": "The last time you checked out"}, {"start": 319.0, "text": "Safari app extensions might've"}, {"start": 321.0, "text": "been in 2016, when we first"}, {"start": 323.0, "text": "introduced them."}, {"start": 324.0, "text": "As you can see from what we"}, {"start": 325.0, "text": "covered today, we've added a lot"}, {"start": 328.0, "text": "of functionality and APIs since"}, {"start": 329.0, "text": "then."}, {"start": 330.0, "text": "If you haven't converted your"}, {"start": 332.0, "text": "Legacy Safari extension yet,"}, {"start": 334.0, "text": "head on over to our guide on"}, {"start": 335.0, "text": "developer.apple.com."}, {"start": 337.0, "text": "And that's improvements to"}, {"start": 340.0, "text": "Safari extensions."}, {"start": 344.0, "text": "Lastly, I want to talk about"}, {"start": 345.0, "text": "following links on macOS."}, {"start": 347.0, "text": "I'm of course talking about"}, {"start": 350.0, "text": "following links like these to"}, {"start": 352.0, "text": "websites and apps."}, {"start": 355.0, "text": "For those of you bringing your"}, {"start": 356.0, "text": "iPad apps to the Mac, you might"}, {"start": 358.0, "text": "be wondering how this is going"}, {"start": 359.0, "text": "to work."}, {"start": 361.0, "text": "In-app web browsing isn't common"}, {"start": 362.0, "text": "on macOS, but it is on iOS."}, {"start": 365.0, "text": "And on iOS, you're probably"}, {"start": 367.0, "text": "using SafariViewController for"}, {"start": 369.0, "text": "the best in-app web browsing"}, {"start": 370.0, "text": "experience."}, {"start": 372.0, "text": "When you open a link in"}, {"start": 374.0, "text": "SafariViewController in your Mac"}, {"start": 375.0, "text": "app, it does exactly what your"}, {"start": 377.0, "text": "macOS users will expect."}, {"start": 379.0, "text": "It opens the link directly in"}, {"start": 381.0, "text": "their browser, and immediately"}, {"start": 382.0, "text": "calls SafariViewController did"}, {"start": 384.0, "text": "finish to notify you."}, {"start": 386.0, "text": "For those of you who have"}, {"start": 388.0, "text": "implemented custom in-app web"}, {"start": 390.0, "text": "browser on iOS, you should"}, {"start": 392.0, "text": "strongly instead consider"}, {"start": 394.0, "text": "directly opening links on Mac,"}, {"start": 396.0, "text": "so that they open in the user's"}, {"start": 397.0, "text": "web browser."}, {"start": 398.0, "text": "That's what your macOS users"}, {"start": 399.0, "text": "will be expecting."}, {"start": 403.0, "text": "We're also excited that"}, {"start": 404.0, "text": "universal links are coming to"}, {"start": 405.0, "text": "macOS this year."}, {"start": 407.0, "text": "On iOS and macOS, universal"}, {"start": 409.0, "text": "links allow you to have ordinary"}, {"start": 412.0, "text": "HTTPS URLs to your website open"}, {"start": 414.0, "text": "in your app instead, if it's"}, {"start": 415.0, "text": "installed."}, {"start": 416.0, "text": "It's way better than custom URL"}, {"start": 419.0, "text": "schemes, which just don't work"}, {"start": 421.0, "text": "if your app isn't installed."}, {"start": 425.0, "text": "Universal links on Mac initially"}, {"start": 426.0, "text": "open in your web browser, just"}, {"start": 428.0, "text": "like before, and when they open"}, {"start": 430.0, "text": "in Safari and your app is"}, {"start": 431.0, "text": "installed, Safari will show a"}, {"start": 433.0, "text": "banner at the top of the"}, {"start": 434.0, "text": "webpage."}, {"start": 436.0, "text": "There, the user can choose to"}, {"start": 438.0, "text": "open the link in your app, and"}, {"start": 440.0, "text": "if they do, future link follows"}, {"start": 442.0, "text": "will be open directly in your"}, {"start": 443.0, "text": "app."}, {"start": 446.0, "text": "To learn more about universal"}, {"start": 448.0, "text": "links, check out the video we"}, {"start": 449.0, "text": "made, available right now in the"}, {"start": 451.0, "text": "WWDC app."}, {"start": 455.0, "text": "And that's following links on"}, {"start": 456.0, "text": "macOS."}, {"start": 457.0, "text": "There have been a bunch of great"}, {"start": 460.0, "text": "improvements in the intersection"}, {"start": 462.0, "text": "of app development and web"}, {"start": 464.0, "text": "technologies this year."}, {"start": 465.0, "text": "One last point I want to leave"}, {"start": 468.0, "text": "you with."}, {"start": 470.0, "text": "We're committed to making Safari"}, {"start": 471.0, "text": "app extensions and content"}, {"start": 473.0, "text": "blockers better each year."}, {"start": 474.0, "text": "If you had previously checked"}, {"start": 476.0, "text": "them out but found that a"}, {"start": 477.0, "text": "particular API or capability was"}, {"start": 479.0, "text": "missing, it's worth taking"}, {"start": 481.0, "text": "another look and converting your"}, {"start": 483.0, "text": "Legacy Safari extension."}, {"start": 484.0, "text": "To find out more about what we"}, {"start": 488.0, "text": "covered today, check out the"}, {"start": 490.0, "text": "WWDC app, where there'll be"}, {"start": 491.0, "text": "links to resources we talked"}, {"start": 492.0, "text": "about and further documentation."}, {"start": 495.0, "text": "And if you have any questions"}, {"start": 496.0, "text": "right now, we'll be headed over"}, {"start": 498.0, "text": "to Technology Lab 3."}, {"start": 500.0, "text": "We'd love to see you there."}, {"start": 502.0, "text": "Thank you so much and have a"}]}